			</div>

			<div class="section">
				<div class="container">
					<div class="text-center mb-5" data-aos="zoom-in" data-aos-delay="100">
						<h2>Supercharge Your Compliancy Programs</h2>
					</div>

					<div class="row justify-content-center g-4">
						<div class="col-12" data-aos="fade-down" data-aos-delay="200">
							<div id="backflow-program" class="info-box steelblue">
								<div class="row justify-content-center align-items-center g-2">
									<div class="col-auto">
										<i class="fa-solid fa-gauge-high"></i>
									</div>
									<div class="col-auto">
										<h3>Backflow Assembly Tracking</h3>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="content">
									<p>
										Envirotrax&reg; provides user-friendly online tools for entering backflow test and
										maintenance reports and performing regular periodic testing of assemblies.
										From the initial consultation through the duration of the service contract, cities
										or
										water purveyors incur NO CHARGES for using the system.
										A small fee is paid by the Backflow Prevention Assembly Tester (BPAT) when
										submitting a
										passing test report.
									</p>
									<p>
										Water purveyor personnel can access the system through a password-protected account.
										There are no limits placed on the number of employees who may access the system.
									</p>
									<p>
										Envirotrax&reg; ensures the validity of all BPAT licenses, insurance policies, and
										gauge
										test for accuracy reports. If any credentials expire, testers will be unable to
										submit
										test reports.
										Our advanced letter generation software allows for flexible and customizable
										creation of
										up to three renewal letters, and we handle 100% of the letter generation and
										mailing.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="col-12" data-aos="fade-down" data-aos-delay="300">
							<div id="csi-program" class="info-box cyan">
								<div class="row justify-content-center align-items-center g-2">
									<div class="col-auto">
										<i class="fa-solid fa-building"></i>
									</div>
									<div class="col-auto">
										<h3>Customer Service Inspections (CSI)</h3>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="content">
									<p>
										A Customer Service Inspection (CSI) examines private water distribution facilities
										to
										approve or deny water service, focusing on identifying and preventing
										cross-connections,
										potential contaminant hazards, and illegal lead materials.
									</p>
									<p>
										Envirotrax&reg; offers the online entry of Customer Service Inspection Certificates
										at
										NO CHARGE to cities or water purveyors. A small fee is paid by third-party Customer
										Service Inspectors for each certificate entered, while certificates entered by city
										or
										water purveyor personnel are entered at NO CHARGE.
									</p>
									<p>
										Our system links any cross-connections found during the inspection with existing
										test
										and maintenance reports on backflow assemblies already on file within the system.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="col-12" data-aos="fade-down" data-aos-delay="400">
							<div id="fog-program" class="info-box magenta">
								<div class="row justify-content-center align-items-center g-2">
									<div class="col-auto">
										<i class="fa-solid fa-truck"></i>
									</div>
									<div class="col-auto">
										<h3>FOG Inspections and Waste Disposal</h3>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="content">
									<p>
										FOG, or Fats, Oils, and Grease, are natural by-products of cooking that can solidify
										and
										stick to sewer pipes, causing backups or overflows.
										Regular pumping and inspections of grease and grit traps are necessary to prevent
										these
										issues and determine the required frequency of pumping.
									</p>
									<p>
										Envirotrax&reg; offers a complete system for the online entry, tracking, and
										reporting
										of waste removal and disposal through our FOG program.
										This service is provided at NO CHARGE to cities or water purveyors. A small fee is
										paid
										by the transporter for each trip ticket or manifest entered,
										while inspections performed on grease or grit taps by city or water purveyor
										personnel
										are entered at NO CHARGE.
									</p>
									<p>
										Additional tools help to manage transporter vehicle permits and inspections,
										automatically calculate the 25% rule on FOG inspections, and set future inspection
										due
										dates, follow-ups and more.
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

